From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: lp855x: honour power state and LP8556 register off

Use the standard brightness helper so bl_power, framebuffer blanking and
system sleep all select zero brightness without losing the requested
level. The previous implementation ignored bl_power completely.

In LP8556 register-only mode also clear BL_CTL for zero brightness and
set it when restoring a nonzero level. This explicitly enters the chip's
off state instead of relying on a stopped PWM clock's output level.
Preserve other control bits and the behaviour of PWM mode and other chip
variants.

Reference: TI LP8556 datasheet SNVS871, Device Control register 01h. On
SM-T531, writes of brightness 0 and control 0x84 read back correctly and
physically extinguish the backlight; restoring control 0x85 restores it.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/lp855x_bl.c b/drivers/video/backlight/lp855x_bl.c
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/lp855x_bl.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/lp855x_bl.c
@@ -240,17 +240,25 @@
 static int lp855x_bl_update_status(struct backlight_device *bl)
 {
 	struct lp855x *lp = bl_get_data(bl);
-	int brightness = bl->props.brightness;
-
-	if (bl->props.state & (BL_CORE_SUSPENDED | BL_CORE_FBBLANK))
-		brightness = 0;
+	int brightness = backlight_get_brightness(bl);
+	int ret;
 
 	if (lp->mode == PWM_BASED)
 		return lp855x_pwm_ctrl(lp, brightness,
 				      bl->props.max_brightness);
-	else if (lp->mode == REGISTER_BASED)
-		return lp855x_write_byte(lp, lp->cfg->reg_brightness,
-					(u8)brightness);
+	else if (lp->mode == REGISTER_BASED) {
+		ret = lp855x_write_byte(lp, lp->cfg->reg_brightness,
+				       (u8)brightness);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		/* LP8556 BL_CTL gates the backlight in register-only mode. */
+		if (lp->chip_id == LP8556 &&
+		    (lp->pdata->device_control & GENMASK(2, 1)) == BIT(2))
+			return lp855x_update_bit(lp, LP855X_DEVICE_CTRL, BIT(0),
+						brightness ? BIT(0) : 0);
+		return 0;
+	}
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
